{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age","id":23413,"title":"Dealing with parents, even at my age...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-04T17:57:23-08:00","id":23413,"title":"Dealing with parents, even at my age...","content":"Today, Mom had to go to the thyroid doctor for her yearly checkup (she has a couple of nodes that bear watching). The doctor went ahead and arrange the bloodwork and the ultrasound so we can get everything done in one day. Since we had a couple of hours before the ultrasound, we decided to go find some craft stores. <br /> <br /> No luck.<br /> <br /> Instead, we found a Super Walmart with a good craft section. Picked up canvases, acrylics, pastel chalks and glitter glue so the kids can design their stockings this weekend (depending on the weather). We were leaving the parking lot and she goes south. The imaging center is north. <br /> <br /> When I travel, I use landmarks so I won't get lost. I told her she was going in the wrong direction but she did not listen until we went out of the city and she realize that I was right. She straiten herself out and I got her in the right direction, finally arriving at the center with time to spare.<br /> <br /> I feel I want to mention to the doctor that she is getting a little &quot;strange&quot;. Maybe it is old age, maybe the start of dementia. I have started the routine of making sure she takes her pills, checking her bank account when she is online, controlling the phone for scammers. She is suppose to be my guardian but she is my payee for my disability. Our roles are becoming reversed. My bipolar is pretty leveled out (I still have racing thoughts and sometimes hear voices). I inventory our foodstuffs and make a list, praying we get everything in one trip (I use my SNAP for bread and milk). I get the discounted meats so we can have stews in the slowcooker (I make a mean beef tips).<br /> <br /> I plan to talk to my brother about this. I cannot afford to be taking care of someone who is possibly losing her mind who is suppose to be taking care of me. Next month, I have my Runescape bill due and I play it as part of my therapy when I am not crocheting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T20:48:54-08:00","id":23489,"title":"","content":"My friend's dad just died.<br /> <br /> Don't really know what to say that..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T22:01:20-08:00","id":23534,"title":"","content":"Look, I'm not saying I'm judging the entire scenario based on this, nor should I, but it still must be said:<br /> <br /> It seems ass backwards when someone says they can't afford to be taking care of someone while they are <i>paying to play Runescape</i>.<br /> <br /> Were I to do so, though, I'd have a really hard time sympathizing more so than I already do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T22:49:42-08:00","id":23550,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel better its really hard being an Orphan. I hope your family helps you, I try my best just not to get squished for being the youngest who is impoverished and also has medical problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T06:32:22-08:00","id":23715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age?p=23534#post23534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I'm not saying I'm judging the entire scenario based on this, nor should I, but it still must be said:<br /> <br /> It seems ass backwards when someone says they can't afford to be taking care of someone while they are <i>paying to play Runescape</i>.<br /> <br /> Were I to do so, though, I'd have a really hard time sympathizing more so than I already do.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you consider a reasonable entertainment/mental health budget?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T06:35:31-08:00","id":23717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JadedTrueBrujah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age#post23413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I plan to talk to my brother about this. I cannot afford to be taking care of someone who is possibly losing her mind who is suppose to be taking care of me.</div> </div> </div> </div>How old are you? How old is your mother? This is an unfortunate part of life, but it beats the alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T09:33:39-08:00","id":23800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age?p=23715#post23715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you consider a reasonable entertainment/mental health budget?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling this is a loaded question.<br /> <br /> Look, I personally think Runescape is a pretty bad game, but putting that aside, it's a game you can play for free-it may not be as nice as when you pay for it, but see my initial opinion-you can handle some features missing.<br /> <br /> I'm not about to propose a reasonable entertainment/mental health budget when I have no real knowledge of what's going on-I just find that complaining about having to pay for <i>another human being</i> when you are paying for <i>a game</i> you can play <i>for free</i> seems like a really horrible mentality. I have no idea everything going on or what it's like to live with that, so I freely admit I shouldn't be talking.<br /> <br /> That doesn't stop the basic principles of being a decent person from feeling mighty uncomfortable with what I read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T09:36:23-08:00","id":23801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age?p=23800#post23800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling this is a loaded question.<br /> <br /> Look, I personally think Runescape is a pretty bad game, but putting that aside, it's a game you can play for free-it may not be as nice as when you pay for it, but see my initial opinion-you can handle some features missing.<br /> <br /> I'm not about to propose a reasonable entertainment/mental health budget when I have no real knowledge of what's going on-I just find that complaining about having to pay for <i>another human being</i> when you are paying for <i>a game</i> you can play <i>for free</i> seems like a really horrible mentality. I have no idea everything going on or what it's like to live with that, so I freely admit I shouldn't be talking.<br /> <br /> That doesn't stop the basic principles of being a decent person from feeling mighty uncomfortable with what I read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think eight dollars a month is going to make a meaningful difference in caring for someone who is showing signs of dementia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T09:47:08-08:00","id":23804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age?p=23801#post23801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think eight dollars a month is going to make a meaningful difference in caring for someone who is showing signs of dementia?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not finances I'm worried about. It's just something there in the juxtaposition of two concerns<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JadedTrueBrujah</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I plan to talk to my brother about this. I cannot afford to be taking care of someone who is possibly losing her mind who is suppose to be taking care of me. Next month, I have my Runescape bill due and I play it as part of my therapy when I am not crocheting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's attitude.<br /> <br /> Look, guys, I'm trying not to sound harsh here. I'm trying to tell myself I am seeing the wrong thing here because I only see so much. That doesn't stop the decent parts of me from squirming when I read the way that line is set up. It comes across as really bitter and uncaring,and I don't assume* Jade is any of that, but it still reads like that.<br /> <br /> *Although, to be fair, I've never read anything from Jade about her(?) mother that wasn't complaining. Again, totally understandable, but you can see why it makes me worry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T10:06:43-08:00","id":23814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age?p=23804#post23804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, guys, I'm trying not to sound harsh here. I'm trying to tell myself I am seeing the wrong thing here because I only see so much. That doesn't stop the decent parts of me from squirming when I read the way that line is set up. It comes across as really bitter and uncaring,and I don't assume* Jade is any of that, but it still reads like that.<br /> <br /> *Although, to be fair, I've never read anything from Jade about her(?) mother that wasn't complaining. Again, totally understandable, but you can see why it makes me worry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the sentence was oddly constructed and seemed to convey a degree of self-absorption, but I make it a habit not to criticize the methods people use to keep despair at bay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T10:07:39-08:00","id":23815,"title":"","content":"Thank you Etherial.-_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T11:55:01-08:00","id":23872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno... I'm not commenting on any specifics that have been mentioned thus far in this thread, but I think that there are definitely methods that are deserving of criticism.<br /> <br /> The obvious would be non-prescription chemical dependencies; narcotics, depressive drinking, off-label pill consumption.<br /> <br /> I think it could certainly apply to anything that is similarly self destructive, especially if it is exacerbating an underlying condition or situation. As a direct, personal, example- I should never play Magic the Gathering. Seems like a relatively innocent thing, but it was my indulgence of choice for years (from high-school through college). To the point where I was stealing food from my roommates and barely making rent because I was spending all my money on cards.<br /> <br /> The specifics are... well, specific. Just where the line gets drawn between an acceptable, healthy hobby and an irresponsible indulgence will vary depending on the exact circumstances of an individual situation. I acknowledge that a message board may not be the best place to get a clear picture of what another person's situation is... although the more <i>sharing</i> someone does, the sharper the image will be. I definitely think that there can be criticisms levied against an activity that damages some other area of a person's life, though. Especially if it's negatively impacting something that seems like it should be a higher priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, with the cardboard crack. When the owner of the store tells you to control your spending, you have a problem. Oddly, other CCGs are just fine for me. That's why I make it a habit, but not a rule, to not criticize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:16:23-08:00","id":24006,"title":"","content":"It's not realistic to have to take care of someone with dementia on your own.. My family has been there and done that. My Gran's mother was still the one to appear running around and then standing at the front door with no clothes on and no idea how she got there...then another case of that with her supposedly trying to take a bath. Money isn't the only problem you will have taking care of someone like that.<br /> <br /> I don't quite see the issue of paying a few dollars for something that is helping one to calm down and stay sane since only a few dollars a month for however many hundreds or more it will cost to keep caring for someone that is not fully mentally aware.<br /> <br /> Having mental problems and then having to care for someone that is slowly and heartbreakingly breaking down themselves also puts a lot of stress on the caregiver, especially if they are family. That will only put you in worse condition. <br /> <br /> Now the rest of this nonsense in this thread *glances at Arc* is just downright rude. If you don't know what's going on in someone's life, why judge so damn harshly?<br /> <br /> Now everyone grab a cup of tea or something and remain calm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i><span style=\"color:darkred\">Got an angel on the left hand and a devil on the right<br /> She's gonna raise a little hell up in heaven tonight---Vixen</span></i></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:olive\"><i>When you say it's all divine and meant to be<br /> What about your flesh and blood and defiers like me?---Avantasia</i></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/821-rayvin-miyu","name":"Rayvin Miyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:25:21-08:00","id":24016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rayvin Miyu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age?p=24006#post24006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having mental problems and then having to care for someone that is slowly and heartbreakingly breaking down themselves also puts a lot of stress on the caregiver, especially if they are family. That will only put you in worse condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember hearing the term &quot;compassion fatigue&quot; for this, and I feel like that really sums up how dealing with serious problems weighs on people. You care about someone, you do anything you can to ease those problems, but that stuff just grinds you down over time. It exhausts you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:31:49-08:00","id":24020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/23413-dealing-with-parents-even-at-my-age?p=24016#post24016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember hearing the term &quot;compassion fatigue&quot; for this, and I feel like that really sums up how dealing with serious problems weighs on people. You care about someone, you do anything you can to ease those problems, but that stuff just grinds you down over time. It exhausts you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! &gt;.&lt; ...and you also have to end up pretty much locking them in your house because they can't live by themselves and have to try explaining several times a day as to why it has to be like that. They get up and leave whenever you least expect it and you could very well lose them forever because of it. Doctors and nurses know more of how to take care of these people than most others....we ended up having to put my Mamaw in a nursing home and visited her as much as we could...still brought things for her when allowed, and so on. She still cried like she did at the house, because she didn't understand why she couldn't go back to her home no matter how many times she had tried to leave my Gran's home and the nursing home. From what we could find, she wasn't being mistreated or abused.....she was given a lot of care and a lot of the free time that the nurses had ( they still would have their meals with some and talk to them and just...be there...for them ).<br /> <br /> It takes a dang team to take care of someone that can't take care of themselves...you can only do so much and it's terrifying and heartbreaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i><span style=\"color:darkred\">Got an angel on the left hand and a devil on the right<br /> She's gonna raise a little hell up in heaven tonight---Vixen</span></i></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:olive\"><i>When you say it's all divine and meant to be<br /> What about your flesh and blood and defiers like me?---Avantasia</i></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/821-rayvin-miyu","name":"Rayvin Miyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T04:36:47-08:00","id":24286,"title":"","content":"We are NOT putting her in a home. The farm is paid for, she can care for herself pretty much, its the slips of her mind I am concerned about. She is concerned about some numbness on her right check, making me think she is experiencing either Bell's palsy or a very mild TIA. I used to be a respite worker for one of my best friends (she had a special needs child and was going to UT for her degree in social work). I go to Austin to rest with Elisabeth, go to movies or play bingo every so often. Runescape is my escape, I play it next to Mom and when I start cussing, she knows I am probably fighting on there or my herbs died (I get more play with the membership...I need to work on my questing and skilling, especially farming). She does not get into Doctor Who like I am. I also maintain a Club Pogo membership for the both of us...she has her games and I have mine.<br /> <br /> I just hate arguing with her when she is wrong. I admit that I am wrong at times but she does not realize it until it is almost too late. She wonders why I am on the computer all the time...it is my addiction. It is part of my illness and if I am not doing something, I get edgy.<br /> <br /> Caring for one's parents is a handful. She retired 2 years ago and sometimes her body stays up all night (she used to do graveyard shift at the hospital). If I get up early and see her on the computer, I know it is going to be a rough day. I catch her snoozing in her chair at times. She tries to take walks except when the weather prevents it (she broke her fibula in May and I had to nurse her until the doctor said it was safe to walk).<br /> <br /> Yesterday was my brother's anniversary and she went to the store to get some food so my SIL can cook up a special meal. The meat section was out of our usual 93/7 hamburger meat and I started grabbing the 1 pound tubes of the same meat at a dollar cheaper. She tried to raise caine but I told her that is it the same thing and we are going to get it that way from now on. Besides, more space in the freezer.<br /> <br /> I pay rent to her to help out with the bills. Depending on the weather, the electric varies, we pay for 2 trash pickup (my brother's and ours), life insurance, car insurance and Tuesday the car tags. I get SNAP and we use that for mainly bread and milk unless I see some meat discounted (that is how we get our steaks, boneless ribs, boneless pork chops and stew meat).<br /> <br /> It is just hard...I am putting of getting V20 book until I payoff one bill (a Christmas present...mattress pad and firm feather pillows). I got her a jigsaw puzzle for Christmas (keeps her mind active). Make-up for Elisabeth and Bella, my niece. <br /> <br /> I am dealing with my self as well...bipolar, PTSD, gout, fibromyalgia, possible borderline disorder...I am being treated and get SSI. So far, the meds are working and I am usually mellow unless someone or something triggers me. If I get triggered, I go to my room and practice some breathing exercises or just lay down.<br /> <br /> Just took my morning pills and expecting the Lasix to kick in...damn edema...THANKS DAD!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T06:30:26-08:00","id":24331,"title":"","content":"You're a lot nicer to your mother than I ever was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T13:57:44-08:00","id":25335,"title":"","content":"I'll return to this when I'm not studying for a make-or-break final, but: <br /> * caregiver role fatigue/strain is absolutely a real thing, and it can wreck families if it's not managed/cared for. Self care, when taking care of a family member, is vital in reducing that strain. <br /> * memory issues can be caused by a WIDE variety of things, but do tend to get progressively worse with aging. <br /> * there are many options and ways regarding management of symptoms and minimizing risks; I can run some of those late next week, if you'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Scathach of the White Wolf forums. Still my pretty, one-winged ducky face, though.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/980-daffiroth","name":"Daffiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar980_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T22:41:08-08:00","id":25614,"title":"","content":"I haven't said anything because I've been trying to PM ArcaneArts for a few days now, which is how I'd have preferred to handle this. Unfortunately, I can't do that. Some forum bug says I have too many PMs to be allowed to send any more, which is pretty much a lie since I have zero PMs, but that's not really the point. The point is, I wouldn't be saying this publicly if I felt I had any other choice. I do not want to throw any more fuel onto this fire, but since ArcaneArts is a friend and I worry that my silence could be taken as disapproval, I will say (and will say only this, because I think any further comments would only make things worse) that I found the original post in this thread shocking in its tone, and I understand where he came from in his response to it.<br /> <br /> My apologies for stoking the flames. For all it's worth, this post is intended to be for and about ArcaneArts, and not anyone else involved or referenced in the discussion.<br /> <br /> I really wish I could have just PMed him this, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T17:06:14-08:00","id":26143,"title":"","content":"If you want a gamer friend to talk to on Runescape, I'm Malekahtepes on there =) Don't worry, I'm not a beggy noob or anything haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title"